csv:     table-3-grady-aspect-ratio-counts.csv
source:  ../source.pdf p.9 (journal page 167), Table 3
anchor:  The calculation of aspect ratios for Grady

# Felix, Colwill & Harris (2022), Defence Technology 18:159-169.
# Grady's Fig. 10 fragment photograph, counted by aspect-ratio bin and by the
# authors' five size Groups. The five Group rows are transcribed here; the
# published Total and Percentage rows are NOT data -- they are the closure,
# expressed as total: checks below, so a mis-keyed count cannot hide.

# Every Group's bins sum to its own stated total.
row:  (n_1to1 + n_1to2 + n_1to3 + n_1to4plus) / total == 1 within 0.001

# The five Groups reproduce the published Total row, bin by bin.
total:  n_1to1     == 1382 within 0.5
total:  n_1to2     == 712  within 0.5
total:  n_1to3     == 303  within 0.5
total:  n_1to4plus == 18   within 0.5
total:  total      == 2415 within 0.5
